  "note": "Annual election of one third (five seats), polled Wednesday 15 January 1930. The five retiring members were renominated (\"all Unionists\") and were opposed by G. A. Anderson and Joseph Holland, both former councillors (elected as Unionist nominees in 1923; their labels in 1930 are not given); Thomas Stevenson's nomination was disallowed (Belfast News-Letter, 8 January 1930, p. 9). Of an electorate of 4,657, 2,080 votes were recorded (about 40 per cent); 34 spoilt."
